# USI-01 Reality Intake source evidence.
#
# The BYTES of every external artifact SIMPROK receives are retained on disk
# under this path (LAW 2.2 — raw truth never disappears), keyed by workspace and
# checksum. It is runtime evidence, not source: it holds real uploaded supplier
# and government documents, and committing it would put customer data in git.
# Overridable via INTAKE_STORAGE_DIR.
backend/storage/

# Owner acceptance workbooks and any other spreadsheet left at the repository
# root. These are real business data — supplier and government price lists —
# placed here for rehearsal, never source. Committing one would put customer
# data in git permanently, so the door is closed rather than trusted.
/*.xlsx
/*.xls
/*.csv
